From 866593d9735cc6fcf6444b158b0ee2b628a9a0ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 06:40:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/85] aegisos: validate decoy user type, drop
 UnsupportedAppUsage

- DecoyProfileHelper#setDecoyProfile now rejects any decoyUserId that is
  not an existing USER_TYPE_FULL_AEGISOS_DECOY user, closing a gap where
  an ordinary secondary user registered by id would route and switch
  correctly but receive none of Component B/C's identity-leak fixes
  (they key off UserInfo.userType, not the registered id). Found during
  the plan's closing whole-branch review.
- USER_SETUP_COMPLETE write reordered to run after DecoyProfileState is
  durably saved, not before.
- getUsersForUiDisplay: removed @UnsupportedAppUsage, added for a
  brand-new @hide method with no prior reflective callers by
  construction; needlessly widens the non-SDK reflection surface.

config_multiuserSkipKeyguardWhenSwitchingToUnlockedUsers's revert is
dropped from this commit: Duress Unlock final closure squashes the
commit that originally enabled this resource out of history entirely
(it was a dead end -- see the patch-audit doc), so there is nothing
left for this commit to revert. Net effect across the whole series is
unchanged: the resource was never touched.
